<li>Which structure carries the matching chromosome sets after mitosis?</li><li>Where are chromosomes found in a eukaryotic animal cell?</li></ol><p><strong>Today I can:</strong></p><ul><li>I can label DNA, a gene and a chromosome in a simple model.</li><li>I can explain that a gene is a section of DNA with a protein instruction.</li><li>I can distinguish one chromosome from the genome.</li></ul><p data-mbm-guide>All pupils respond; reveal the answers only after attempts. Revisit success criteria.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-i_do"><h2>I do <span class="meta">· 5 min</span></h2><p>Watch the full model. Point to the step that answers today’s question.</p><h3>Words</h3><table class="wordtable"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Word</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">DNA</th><td>the molecule that stores genetic instructions</td><td>DNA contains the instructions for making proteins.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">gene</th><td>a section of DNA that codes for a specific protein</td><td>The coloured section of the model stands for one gene.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">chromosome</th><td>a long DNA molecule packaged with proteins in a cell</td><td>A chromosome contains many DNA sections, including genes.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">genome</th><td>the entire DNA of an organism</td><td>The genome includes all of the organism’s chromosomes and other DNA.</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="card"><strong>Full model:</strong> Mark a short section of a DNA cord as a gene. Coil the cord as one chromosome; place it inside a border for the genome. Name the section, molecule, package and complete DNA set.</p><p><strong>Show me:</strong> Show me: is a gene a section of DNA, or is all DNA inside one gene?</p><p data-mbm-guide>Answer: A gene is a section of DNA.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Model one complete example; check every pupil’s response to the show-me question.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-we_do"><h2>We do <span class="meta">· 7 min</span></h2><p>Complete the missing step in the part-done model. Speak, then match the cards.</p><p class="reset">One-minute reset: use the agreed move, then return to one step.</p><p><strong>Part-done model:</strong> DNA cord → a short marked ________ codes for a protein → chromosome package → the genome contains all DNA.</p><p><strong>Speak first:</strong> Speaking: “A gene is part of …; a chromosome contains …”</p><p class="way">F · support: Use the full cord model; place the gene label on the short marked section.</p><p class="tier">M · explain: Explain how the short DNA section relates to one gene and the larger package.</p><p class="deeper">H · stretch: Explain why “one chromosome = one gene” misrepresents scale and role.</p><div class="sort"><h3>Select where each label belongs in the string model and explain one mismatch.</h3><form id="match-form"><ul><li data-answer="gene"><span>short coloured DNA section</span><label>Match <select aria-label="Match short coloured DNA section"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="DNA">DNA</option><option value="chromosome">chromosome</option><option value="gene">gene</option><option value="genome">genome</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></li><li data-answer="DNA"><span>whole genetic molecule</span><label>Match <select aria-label="Match whole genetic molecule"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="DNA">DNA</option><option value="chromosome">chromosome</option><option value="gene">gene</option><option value="genome">genome</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></li><li data-answer="chromosome"><span>long DNA package</span><label>Match <select aria-label="Match long DNA package"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="DNA">DNA</option><option value="chromosome">chromosome</option><option value="gene">gene</option><option value="genome">genome</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></li><li data-answer="genome"><span>all of the organism’s DNA</span><label>Match <select aria-label="Match all of the organism’s DNA"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="DNA">DNA</option><option value="chromosome">chromosome</option><option value="gene">gene</option><option value="genome">genome</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></li></ul></form><button type="button" id="match-check">Check the matches</button><button type="button" id="match-reset">Start again</button><p class="feedback" id="match-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to match.</p></div><p data-mbm-guide>Wait five seconds, gesture, then cue if needed. Support the route without supplying the missing answer.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-we_do_2"><h2>We do 2 <span class="meta">· 5 min</span></h2><p>Choose one hinge answer. Show it at the same time as the group.</p><div class="hinge"><p><strong>All-pupil hinge:</strong> Which description of a gene is accurate?</p><form><fieldset><legend>Choose one answer</legend><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W04" value="A">A. A section of DNA that codes for a specific protein.</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W04" value="B">B. Every piece of DNA in the whole genome.</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W04" value="C">C. A protein that holds the chromosome together.</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W04" value="D">D. A separate cell outside the chromosome.</label></fieldset><button type="reset">Clear choice</button></form><p>Show one answer to the adult at the same time as everyone else. Point or use a card, too. Then explain to a partner.</p></div><p data-mbm-guide>Collect simultaneous responses, apply the decision rule and parallel hinge in the staff note.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-independent"><h2>Independent <span class="meta">· 8 min</span></h2><p>Two diagrams label a gene differently. Choose the accurate model and explain one reason.</p><p class="reset">One-minute reset: use the agreed move, then return to one step.</p><p><strong>Talk before write:</strong> Speaking: “Move this label because …”</p><p>You can plan in any language.</p><p class="tier"><strong>F:</strong> Label a gene, DNA, chromosome and genome on the model. <em>This short marked section is a …; the long package is a …</em></p><p class="tier"><strong>M:</strong> Explain why a gene is a DNA section, not another material. <em>A gene is part of … and codes for …</em></p><p class="tier"><strong>H:</strong> Correct a faulty gene label and explain the protein instruction. <em>The faulty label is …; it should be … because …</em></p><p class="deeper">Go deeper: What distinctions disappear if the whole genome is called one gene?</p><p class="deeper">Early-finisher stretch — Two-diagram audit: Repair two faulty diagrams: DNA inside a gene, and one chromosome as the entire genome. Justify both.</p><p><strong>Show it your way:</strong> point, sign, speak, draw, type, write, use a scribe or a staff-captured photo.</p><p data-mbm-guide>At lesson start choose one adult with supported pupils and one holding the group; swap during the week. Record independence and prompt level.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-review"><h2>Review <span class="meta">· 4 min</span></h2><p>Tell a partner what you changed after feedback. Mark a real edit // and read it back when asked ?.</p><p class="reset">One-minute reset: use the agreed move, then return to one step.</p><p><strong>My feedback was …</strong> Name the actual point an adult or partner noticed. Make one true self-edit <strong>//</strong>. Ask “Read this back to me” <strong>?</strong> if that helps.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Give a precise VF or NS(+) only when it actually happens. Invite a true self-edit and read-back.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-exit"><h2>Exit <span class="meta">· 3 min</span></h2><p>Show what you know with a model and explain one reason.</p><p><strong>Check today’s success:</strong></p><ul><li>I can label DNA, a gene and a chromosome in a simple model.</li><li>I can explain that a gene is a section of DNA with a protein instruction.</li><li>I can distinguish one chromosome from the genome.</li></ul><p><strong>What am I learning?</strong> I am learning to show how a gene is part of DNA and how DNA is packed into chromosomes.</p><p><strong>My feedback was …</strong> Name what you heard at Review.</p><p><strong>Next I need to …</strong> Use “section of DNA” and “codes for a protein” precisely in one sentence.</p><p><strong>How I know:</strong> I can show a gene within DNA, DNA packaged in a chromosome, and the genome as all DNA.</p><p>Your teacher hears your answer and uses it to choose our next model, prompt or example.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Hear the answer privately in a valid mode and use it to change the next example or prompt.</p></section></main><footer><p>Offline lesson · no answers or scores are stored.</p></footer><script>"use strict";(()=>{const form=document.getElementById('match-form'),out=document.getElementById('match-feedback');document.getElementById('match-check').addEventListener('click',()=>{let blanks=0,good=0;form.querySelectorAll('select').forEach(s=>{const answer=s.closest('[data-answer]').dataset.answer;if(!s.value){blanks++;s.nextElementSibling.textContent='Choose a match.'}else if(s.value===answer){good++;s.nextElementSibling.textContent='That fits. Explain why.'}else s.nextElementSibling.textContent='Check the model and try again.'});out.textContent=blanks?'Choose a match for each card.':good===form.querySelectorAll('select').length?'All matched. Tell a partner your reason.':'Use the model to repair a match.'});document.getElementById('match-reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{form.reset();form.querySelectorAll('output').forEach(x=>x.textContent='');out.textContent='Ready to match.';form.querySelector('select').focus()});})();</script></body></html>
