le" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="18" fill="#17394a" >Aa parent</text><text x="90" y="65" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="17" fill="#17394a" >aa parent</text><rect x="172" y="56" width="132" height="132" rx="2" fill="#fff" stroke="#17394a" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M238 56v132M172 122h132" fill="none" stroke="#17394a" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" /><text x="205.0" y="46" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="19" fill="#17394a" >A</text><text x="271.0" y="46" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="19" fill="#17394a" >a</text><text x="156" y="94.28" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="19" fill="#17394a" >a</text><text x="156" y="160.28" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="19" fill="#17394a" >a</text><text x="205.0" y="96.92" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="19" fill="#17394a" >Aa</text><text x="271.0" y="96.92" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="19" fill="#17394a" >aa</text><text x="205.0" y="162.92000000000002" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="19" fill="#17394a" >Aa</text><text x="271.0" y="162.92000000000002" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="19" fill="#17394a" >aa</text><text x="237" y="218" text-anchor="middle" font-family="Arial,sans-serif" font-size="16" fill="#17394a" >four possible pairs</text></svg><figcaption>Invented A/a flower model: Aa × aa gives two Aa and two aa possibilities. Each square is a possibility, not a family count. Simplified.</figcaption></figure><p data-mbm-guide>Offer a private, predictable start. Do not require previous knowledge.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-starter"><h2>Starter <span class="meta">· 3 min</span></h2><p>Recall three ideas from earlier lessons. Show one answer at a time.</p><ol><li>What is a gene?</li><li>What do stem cells do in growth?</li><li>Where are chromosomes found in an animal cell?</li></ol><p><strong>Today I can:</strong></p><ul><li>I can pair one allele from each parent.</li><li>I can find the aa chance in four squares.</li><li>I can evaluate why probability does not guarantee an exact count.</li></ul><p data-mbm-guide>All pupils respond; reveal the answers only after attempts. Revisit success criteria.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-i_do"><h2>I do <span class="meta">· 5 min</span></h2><p>Watch the full model. Point to the step that answers today’s question.</p><h3>Words</h3><table class="wordtable"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Word</th><th scope="col">Meaning</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">allele</th><td>a version of a gene</td><td>A and a represent two alleles in our invented model.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">genotype</th><td>the pair of alleles shown by letters</td><td>Aa is one possible genotype in this model.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">dominant</th><td>an allele shown by one copy in this simple model</td><td>A is dominant in our invented flower model.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">recessive</th><td>an allele shown when two copies are present in this model</td><td>aa shows the recessive version in our model.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Punnett square</th><td>a grid that shows possible allele pairs</td><td>The Punnett square for Aa × aa has four cells.</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="card"><strong>Full model:</strong> Place A/a atop the grid for one parent; place a/a at its side for the other. Pair one allele from each edge: Aa, aa, Aa, aa. Two of four boxes are aa: a 1 in 2 chance per offspring, not an exact family count.</p><p><strong>Show me:</strong> Show me: which allele can the aa parent pass on?</p><p data-mbm-guide>Answer: Only a.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Model one complete example; check every pupil’s response to the show-me question.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-we_do"><h2>We do <span class="meta">· 7 min</span></h2><p>Complete the missing step in the part-done model. Speak, then match the cards.</p><p class="reset">One-minute reset: use the agreed move, then return to one step.</p><p><strong>Part-done model:</strong> Aa × aa: top A, a; side a, a. First row Aa, aa; second row ___, ___. Chance of aa: ___ out of 4.</p><p><strong>Speak first:</strong> One allele from the top is …; one from the side is …; together they make …</p><p class="way">F · support: Place one letter tile from the top and one from the side into a single square. Point to the next pair.</p><p class="tier">M · explain: Explain why the two aa squares represent half the model outcomes.</p><p class="deeper">H · stretch: Predict the aa chance for Aa × Aa before checking a second model. Explain the change.</p><div class="sort"><h3>Complete the 2 × 2 digital grid. Choose the genotype in each square.</h3><form id="match-form"><table class="wordtable"><caption>Digital Punnett square: one allele from each parent per cell</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">aa × Aa</th><th scope="col">A</th><th scope="col">a</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">a</th><td data-answer="Aa"><label>Row 1, A with a <select aria-label="Row 1, A with a genotype"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="Aa">Aa</option><option value="aa">aa</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></td><td data-answer="aa"><label>Row 1, a with a <select aria-label="Row 1, a with a genotype"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="Aa">Aa</option><option value="aa">aa</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></td></tr><tr><th scope="row">a</th><td data-answer="Aa"><label>Row 2, A with a <select aria-label="Row 2, A with a genotype"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="Aa">Aa</option><option value="aa">aa</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></td><td data-answer="aa"><label>Row 2, a with a <select aria-label="Row 2, a with a genotype"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="Aa">Aa</option><option value="aa">aa</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></td></tr></tbody></table></form><button type="button" id="match-check">Check the grid</button><button type="button" id="match-reset">Start again</button><p class="feedback" id="match-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to match.</p></div><p data-mbm-guide>Wait five seconds, gesture, then cue if needed. Support the route without supplying the missing answer.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-we_do_2"><h2>We do 2 <span class="meta">· 5 min</span></h2><p>Choose one hinge answer. Show it at the same time as the group.</p><div class="hinge"><p><strong>All-pupil hinge:</strong> In the invented Aa × aa model, what is the chance of an aa offspring?</p><form><fieldset><legend>Choose one answer</legend><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W05" value="A">A. 1 in 2.</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W05" value="B">B. 1 in 4.</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W05" value="C">C. Certain: every offspring is aa.</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W05" value="D">D. Impossible: no parent has a.</label></fieldset><button type="reset">Clear choice</button></form><p>Show one answer to the adult at the same time as everyone else. Point or use a card, too. Then explain to a partner.</p></div><p data-mbm-guide>Collect simultaneous responses, apply the decision rule and parallel hinge in the staff note.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-independent"><h2>Independent <span class="meta">· 8 min</span></h2><p>Calculate the aa probability for Aa × aa. Evaluate an exact-count claim about real offspring.</p><p class="reset">One-minute reset: use the agreed move, then return to one step.</p><p><strong>Talk before write:</strong> The chance is … because …; this does not promise …</p><p>You can plan in any language.</p><p cla