cope="row">variant</th><td>a changed version of a gene</td><td>The card describes a changed CFTR variant.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">carrier</th><td>a person with one changed copy in this recessive example</td><td>A carrier usually does not have cystic fibrosis.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">source</th><td>where a claim comes from</td><td>The NHS page is the source for this card.</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="card"><strong>Full model:</strong> The NHS card says cystic fibrosis is inherited. Changed CFTR copies come from both parents. One changed copy usually means a carrier; two usually cause the condition. Name the NHS card with each claim.</p><p><strong>Show me:</strong> Show me: is the genetic cause of cystic fibrosis inherited or passed by brief contact?</p><p data-mbm-guide>Answer: Inherited. This says nothing about infection precautions a person with CF may need.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Model one complete example; check every pupil’s response to the show-me question.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-we_do"><h2>We do <span class="meta">· 7 min</span></h2><p>Complete the missing step in the part-done model. Speak, then match the cards.</p><p class="reset">One-minute reset: use the agreed move, then return to one step.</p><p><strong>Part-done model:</strong> The NHS card says cystic fibrosis is ___. It involves the ___ gene. One changed copy usually means a ___. Source: ___.</p><p><strong>Speak first:</strong> The card names …; this sentence supports …; this line is about …</p><p class="way">F · support: Point to the card’s condition, inheritance and care lines before speaking.</p><p class="tier">M · explain: Explain which card sentence supports inheritance and which sentence describes care.</p><p class="deeper">H · stretch: Use the card to reject the claim that every carrier has symptoms.</p><div class="sort"><h3>Match each short statement to a source-card section.</h3><form id="match-form"><ul><li data-answer="What it is"><span>Can affect breathing and digestion</span><label>Match <select aria-label="Match Can affect breathing and digestion"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="What it is">What it is</option><option value="Inheritance">Inheritance</option><option value="Care">Care</option><option value="Source">Source</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></li><li data-answer="Inheritance"><span>Usually two changed CFTR copies</span><label>Match <select aria-label="Match Usually two changed CFTR copies"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="What it is">What it is</option><option value="Inheritance">Inheritance</option><option value="Care">Care</option><option value="Source">Source</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></li><li data-answer="Care"><span>Treatments help manage symptoms</span><label>Match <select aria-label="Match Treatments help manage symptoms"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="What it is">What it is</option><option value="Inheritance">Inheritance</option><option value="Care">Care</option><option value="Source">Source</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></li><li data-answer="Source"><span>NHS page named and dated</span><label>Match <select aria-label="Match NHS page named and dated"><option value="">Choose…</option><option value="What it is">What it is</option><option value="Inheritance">Inheritance</option><option value="Care">Care</option><option value="Source">Source</option></select><output aria-live="polite"></output></label></li></ul></form><button type="button" id="match-check">Check the matches</button><button type="button" id="match-reset">Start again</button><p class="feedback" id="match-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite">Ready to match.</p></div><p data-mbm-guide>Wait five seconds, gesture, then cue if needed. Support the route without supplying the missing answer.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-we_do_2"><h2>We do 2 <span class="meta">· 5 min</span></h2><p>Choose one hinge answer. Show it at the same time as the group.</p><div class="hinge"><p><strong>All-pupil hinge:</strong> Which source-card statement supports cystic fibrosis as an inherited genetic condition?</p><form><fieldset><legend>Choose one answer</legend><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W06" value="A">A. It involves changed copies of CFTR inherited from parents.</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W06" value="B">B. A changed CFTR copy can spread by sharing a table.</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W06" value="C">C. All lung symptoms are inherited.</label><label><input type="radio" name="hinge-SCI_LAUNCH_A2_W06" value="D">D. Treatment alone proves how it is inherited.</label></fieldset><button type="reset">Clear choice</button></form><p>Show one answer to the adult at the same time as everyone else. Point or use a card, too. Then explain to a partner.</p></div><p data-mbm-guide>Collect simultaneous responses, apply the decision rule and parallel hinge in the staff note.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-independent"><h2>Independent <span class="meta">· 8 min</span></h2><p>Present three sourced facts from the offline NHS card, then correct an unsupported claim.</p><p class="reset">One-minute reset: use the agreed move, then return to one step.</p><p><strong>Talk before write:</strong> My source is …; it supports …; it does not tell us …</p><p>You can plan in any language.</p><p class="tier"><strong>F:</strong> State the condition and one fact with the NHS source named. <em>The card says …; the source is …</em></p><p class="tier"><strong>M:</strong> Explain CFTR inheritance and separate it from infection. <em>The CFTR change is inherited because …; infection advice is separate because …</em></p><p class="tier"><strong>H:</strong> Revise an unsupported claim with the NHS card. <em>The claim is not supported by …; I would revise it to …</em></p><p class="deeper">Go deeper: Why does one changed copy in this example not justify saying a carrier has the condition?</p><p class="deeper">Early-finisher stretch — Source claim audit: Repair a draft saying a CFTR change spreads by touch and outcomes are fixed; source both repairs.</p><p><strong>Show it your way:</strong> point, sign, speak, draw, type, write, use a scribe or a staff-captured photo.</p><p data-mbm-guide>At lesson start choose one adult with supported pupils and one holding the group; swap during the week. Record independence and prompt level.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-review"><h2>Review <span class="meta">· 4 min</span></h2><p>Tell a partner what you changed after feedback. Mark a real edit // and read it back when asked ?.</p><p class="reset">One-minute reset: use the agreed move, then return to one step.</p><p><strong>My feedback was …</strong> Name the actual point an adult or partner noticed. Make one true self-edit <strong>//</strong>. Ask “Read this back to me” <strong>?</strong> if that helps.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Give a precise VF or NS(+) only when it actually happens. Invite a true self-edit and read-back.</p></section><section class="stage" id="stage-exit"><h2>Exit <span class="meta">· 3 min</span></h2><p>Show what you know with a model and explain one reason.</p><p><strong>Check today’s success:</strong></p><ul><li>I can name the condition and source.</li><li>I can explain CFTR inheritance without personal details.</li><li>I can tell a sourced fact from a guess.</li></ul><p><strong>What am I learning?</strong> I am learning to use a named source to present careful facts about a genetic condition.</p><p><strong>My feedback was …</strong> Name what you heard at Review.</p><p><strong>Next I need to …</strong> Put the NHS source next to each scientific claim.</p><p><strong>How I know:</strong> I can give accurate CFTR facts, name the NHS card and correct an unsupported claim.</p><p>Your teacher hears your answer and uses it to choose our next model, prompt or example.</p><p data-mbm-guide>Hear the answer privately in a valid mode and use it to change the next example or prompt.</p></section></main><footer><p>Offline lesson · no answers or scores are stored.</p></footer><script>"use strict";(()=>{const form=document.getElementById('match-form'),out=document.getElementById('match-feedback');document.getElementById('match-check').addEventListener('click',()=>{let blanks=0,good=0;form.querySelectorAll('select').forEach(s=>{const answer=s.closest('[data-answer]').dataset.answer;if(!s.value){blanks++;s.nextElementSibling.textContent='Choose a match.'}else if(s.value===answer){good++;s.nextElementSibling.textContent='That fits. Explain why.'}else s.nextElementSibling.textContent='Check the model and try again.'});out.textContent=blanks?'Choose a match for each card.':good===form.querySelectorAll('select').length?'All matched. Tell a partner your reason.':'Use the model to repair a match.'});document.getElementById('match-reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{form.reset();form.querySelectorAll('output').forEach(x=>x.textContent='');out.textContent='Ready to match.';form.querySelector('select').focus()});})();</script></body></html>
